<title>FRANCE: France to sell 23 to 25 bln Ffr of OATs Thursday.</title>
<headline>France to sell 23 to 25 bln Ffr of OATs Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>France is to offer between 23 and 25 billion francs of government bonds (OATs) at its next scheduled auction on March 6, the Treasury said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Treasury will offer the current 10-year benchmark OAT, the 5.50 percent April 25, 2007 OAT, with a payment date of March 25, the statement said.</p>
<p>The Treasury said on February 26 it would also be selling a new January 25, 2009 variable rate OAT based on the TEC 10 index at the March 6 auction. It said the new TEC 10 bond would make up between eight and 10 billion francs of the total.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
